Drop the diagnostic-suppressing pragmas that R CMD check notes

R CMD check reports every file containing `#pragma GCC|clang diagnostic
ignored` ("Files which contain pragma(s) suppressing diagnostics"), and a
CRAN reviewer may ask for them to go. Three upstream files carry them:

  src/dispatcher.c                           push/ignore/pop of
                                             -Wunused-parameter and
                                             -Wunused-function around the
                                             fat-runtime dispatch stubs.
  src/util/arch/ppc64el/simd_utils.h         push/ignore/pop of
  src/util/supervector/arch/ppc64el/impl.cpp -Wdeprecate-lax-vec-conv-all,
                                             clang on ppc64el only.

Only the pragma lines (and the #if blocks that exist to hold them) are
removed; no code changes. Without them the compiler may print those
warnings during installation, which is harmless: the bundled build runs
with -Wno-error (see 0002), and none of them is among the warnings
R CMD check treats as significant.

Local, not upstream.

